        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0624" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.156/243</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kreech</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 25.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 421</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Asunción Port
                    Concession, I have the honor to report that, on October 20th, the President
                    signed the law, passed at the last session of Congress, granting a concession to
                    the Asunción Port Concession Corporation.</p>
                <p>The Corporation’s representative, Mr. H. C. Mitchell, is obtaining the data
                    necessary for the drafting of plans and is attending to the preliminaries for an
                    early construction.</p>
                <p>There is a general feeling of optimism and the desire for American capital to
                    undertake the construction of a water works and sewage system, and needed
                    railway extensions.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. L. Kreeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
